# Local mockups — sketches that belong to the machine that made them. The
# sidebar is built from whatever folders are present, so yours show up for you
# and for nobody else. `realtime-refinement` is the committed exception: it is
# the README for the directory, and it explains the rest.
src/routes/mockups/*
!src/routes/mockups/realtime-refinement/
# Not a sketch: the tool that fills in and copies the emails in $lib/email.
!src/routes/mockups/emails/
# Everything below is un-ignored for a load-bearing reason beyond wanting it
# committed: Tailwind v4's source detection SKIPS gitignored files, so a mockup
# that styles itself with utility classes (rather than a scoped <style>) gets
# none of them generated and renders unstyled. Any mockup carrying Tailwind
# classes has to be visible to git.
#
# The card work: the faces are Tailwind all the
# way down, and half the type scale silently rendered at 16px because the only
# arbitrary values that survived were the ones some tracked file happened to use
# too.
!src/routes/mockups/breach-cards/
!src/routes/mockups/glass-exposure/
# Same reason: these are built almost entirely from utility classes.
!src/routes/mockups/agent-installer/
# Committed for a different reason than the two above: `agent-select` is not a
# sketch that stayed on one machine. It is the design the breach lobby was
# ported from, and `examples/breach/lobby/` is a committed implementation of it
# — so the mockup is the reference the real screen is read against, and a
# reference nobody else can open is not one.
!src/routes/mockups/agent-select/
!src/routes/mockups/breach-verdict/
# The vendor profile pair — `vendor-profile` reproduces the shipped page as the
# BEFORE, `vendor-profile-v2` is the redesign read against it. Both are lifted
# straight from app-ui and are utility classes end to end, so the Tailwind rule
# above applies; a comparison where one side renders unstyled proves nothing.
!src/routes/mockups/vendor-profile/
!src/routes/mockups/vendor-profile-v2/
!src/routes/mockups/vendor-profile-v3/

# Before/after storyboard of the sign-in and alpha flows, committed with the fix
# it pictures so the PR's reviewers can open it. Utility classes, so the
# Tailwind rule above applies too.
!src/routes/mockups/login-fix-flow/

# The alpha front page. Committed because it is the reference the marketing site
# is built against, not a scratch sketch — and because the pipeline animation in
# it is a component other pages are likely to want.
!src/routes/mockups/marketing-landing/

# Utility-class mockups the static validator refused while ignored — the
# Tailwind reason above.
!src/routes/mockups/alpha-welcome-email/
!src/routes/mockups/capability-menus/
!src/routes/mockups/date-select/
!src/routes/mockups/hype-cycle-scorecard/
!src/routes/mockups/magic-quadrant-scorecard/
!src/routes/mockups/product-roadmap/
# A 440 KB copy of app-ui's generated API island; it would only ever be stale.
src/routes/docs/api/api.data.json

# Marker for `make showcase-install`; its whole job is to carry the mtime of the
# last npm ci. Committing it (which we did) makes that mtime the CHECKOUT time in
# CI, so make compares two files written seconds apart and decides the install is
# up to date — against an empty node_modules. Whether the install ran at all came
# down to sub-second ordering during checkout.
.install-stamp

# Playwright scratch screenshots — throwaway output from verifying a screen
# locally.
.shots/

# macOS Finder metadata.
.DS_Store

# The breach rules engine and the agent harness, compiled to wasm. Built outside
# this repo (armornet's `make build-breach-wasm`), which also installs the
# matching `wasm_exec` shim straight out of the Go/TinyGo toolchain — so the
# shim is generated too, and `make clean` deletes both.
*.wasm
examples/breach/public/wasm_exec.js
examples/breach/public/wasm_exec_tinygo.js

# One-off Playwright drivers — written to check a single screen once and never
# run again. Same rule as .shots/ above: they belong to the machine that wrote
# them, not to the repo.
/d.mjs
/breach-verify.mjs
**/overlay-tmp.mjs

# The dev console bundle compose/devcog embeds. Built output like any other
# dist, except its .gitkeep: `//go:embed all:dist` does not compile without the
# directory, so a checkout that never ran the build must still carry it.
!compose/devcog/dist/
compose/devcog/dist/*
!compose/devcog/dist/.gitkeep
